Article 2 (Qualifications of Technical Examiners)
(1) Technical examiners shall be appointed as Grade 4 or Grade 5 court officials or as public officials dispatched pursuant to Article 6.
(2) Technical examiners shall be appointed from among persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs. <Amended on December 14, 2005>
1. A person who has served as a patent examiner or trial examiner at the Korean Intellectual Property Office for at least five years;
2. A person who has served in a general-service national public official position involving industrial technology or science and technology for at least seven years, including at least five years in a Grade 5 or higher position;
3. A person who holds a master's degree in a field of science and technology and has engaged in practice or research in that field for at least ten years;
4. A person who holds a doctoral degree in a field of science and technology;
5. A person qualified as a professional engineer under the National Technical Qualifications Act;
6. An attorney-at-law or patent attorney who holds a bachelor's degree in a field of science and technology.
